{
  "about": "Situations in which a manuscript's lines must show on the right page. Each scenario is run by src/test/alignment/scenarios.test.js against the real stores, the real import, the key migration and the Manuscripts view's own composable. 'manuscript' takes the canvas labels and transcription folios of that manuscript from fixtures/iiif/corpus-manifests.json (the real manifest); 'labels' gives them by hand. 'stored' is what an earlier version left in browser storage; 'importFile' is imported through Settings → Import. Under 'expect': 'canvas' = folio -> the IIIF label of the scan shown; 'lines' = folio -> the line regions the Manuscripts view lists; 'keys' = the stored page keys afterwards; 'kept' = how many keys were left for a person to look at; 'drift' = folio -> { line name: the scan it was drawn on }.",
